---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Otherwise Hyperarchive — Micol Gelsi">
<article class="hyperarchive" id="top">
  <div class="hyper-top"><span>EMAP RESIDENCY PROPOSAL / ARTISTIC RESEARCH / WEB + PUBLIC SPACE</span><a href={base}>← PORTFOLIO</a></div>
  <header class="hyper-hero"><span>RESEARCH ATLAS / 2027</span><h1>OTHERWISE<br/>HYPERARCHIVE<span class="hyper-accent">_</span></h1><p>A rhizomatic digital infrastructure for cultivating relationships in physical space.</p><small>PARTICIPATORY ARCHIVING ↔ CRITICAL MAPPING ↔ COLLECTIVE SPACE</small></header>
  <nav class="hyper-nav" aria-label="Proposal sections"><a href="#concept">01 CONCEPT</a><a href="#system">02 SYSTEM</a><a href="#space">03 SPACE</a><a href="#process">04 PROCESS</a><a href="#references">05 REFERENCES</a></nav>
  <section id="concept" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">01 / RESEARCH QUESTION</span><div><h2>What if an archive were an architecture of relationships?</h2><p>OTHERWISE HYPERARCHIVE explores the archive not as a fixed repository, but as a distributed and evolving infrastructure connecting situated knowledge, collective memory, spontaneous urban ecologies and practices of self-organisation.</p><p>Emerging from <em>Archive of the Untamed</em>, the project investigates what institutional classifications of urban space leave unrecorded: relationships of care, everyday forms of collective inhabitation and the memories carried by communities.</p><p>Rather than claiming to preserve or resolve these fragile conditions, the research asks how an accessible, collectively shaped digital system might create occasions for encounter, experimentation and shared use beyond the screen.</p></div></section>
  <section id="system" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">02 / DIGITAL INFRASTRUCTURE</span><div><h2>A non-linear archive</h2><p>The interface is imagined as a rhizomatic network: contributions can connect across places, practices, stories and media without being reduced to a single taxonomy. The web platform is developed with participants, rather than simply presented to them.</p><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 01 — NETWORK / NON-HIERARCHICAL CONNECTIONS</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 380" role="img" aria-label="Rhizomatic archive network"><g class="wires"><path d="M450 184Q250 20 154 100M450 184Q680 12 758 92M450 184Q730 340 768 290M450 184Q210 365 145 292M154 100Q440 10 758 92M145 292Q460 330 768 290M154 100Q90 200 145 292M758 92Q850 180 768 290"/></g><g class="nodes"><circle cx="450" cy="184" r="51"/><circle cx="154" cy="100" r="35"/><circle cx="758" cy="92" r="35"/><circle cx="145" cy="292" r="35"/><circle cx="768" cy="290" r="35"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="450" y="169">HYPER</text><text x="450" y="181">ARCHIVE</text><text x="154" y="104">MEMORY</text><text x="758" y="96">ECOLOGIES</text><text x="145" y="296">SITES</text><text x="768" y="294">COMMUNITIES</text></g></svg></figure><small>Links are relational, revisable and multiple. Diagram is conceptual, not a data visualisation.</small></div></section>
  <section id="space" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">03 / SPATIAL TRANSLATION</span><div><h2>From interface to situated encounter</h2><p>The digital system is brought into public space through two complementary artistic languages. The physical interventions also generate new encounters and contributions that can reshape the archive.</p><div class="hyper-columns"><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 02 — PROJECTION MAPPING</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Projection mapping onto a facade"><g class="wires"><path d="M85 72H315V258H85ZM112 98H176V154H112ZM220 98H283V154H220ZM112 180H176V236H112ZM220 180H283V236H220Z"/></g><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M30 265L112 98L283 154L390 265M30 265L112 236L283 98L390 265"/></g><text x="17" y="285">PROJECTOR</text></svg></figure><h3>01 / Projection mapping</h3><p>Archival fragments, cartographies and audiovisual contributions become temporary layers on existing urban surfaces.</p></div><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 03 — PARASITIC ARCHITECTURE</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Temporary reversible architecture"><g class="wires"><path d="M35 55H170V265H35ZM60 80H145V160H60ZM0 265H420"/></g><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M170 120L250 85L360 135L280 170ZM170 120V225L280 275V170M280 275L360 230V135M250 85V195L360 230M170 225L250 195L280 275"/></g><text x="195" y="57">REVERSIBLE</text><text x="195" y="70">ATTACHMENT</text></svg></figure><h3>02 / Parasitic architectures</h3><p>Lightweight, reversible spatial devices respond to existing structures, opening possibilities for temporary gathering, interaction and collective use.</p></div></div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 04 — RECIPROCAL FEEDBACK LOOP</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 220" role="img" aria-label="Digital archive, spatial interfaces and public encounters feedback loop"><g class="accent-wires"><rect x="48" y="77" width="210" height="65"/><rect x="345" y="77" width="210" height="65"/><rect x="642" y="77" width="210" height="65"/><path d="M258 110H345M555 110H642M747 77Q747 25 450 25Q153 25 153 77"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="153" y="106">DIGITAL ARCHIVE</text><text x="450" y="106">SPATIAL INTERFACES</text><text x="747" y="106">PUBLIC ENCOUNTERS</text><text x="450" y="17">CONTRIBUTIONS RETURN / SYSTEM EVOLVES</text></g></svg></figure></div></section>
  <section id="process" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">04 / TWO-MONTH RESIDENCY</span><div><h2>Research through collaboration and prototyping</h2><div class="hyper-steps"><p><strong>W01–02</strong>Local research, encounters with communities and collaborating artist; collective assessment of the existing archive.</p><p><strong>W03–04</strong>Participatory interface redesign, critical mapping, sketches and spatial prototypes.</p><p><strong>W05–06</strong>Web development, fabrication, projection tests and digital–physical integration.</p><p><strong>W07–08</strong>Situated testing, adaptation, documentation and public presentation.</p></div><div class="hyper-columns"><div><h3>Artist contribution</h3><p>Web development, creative coding, audiovisual production, projection-mapping workflow and laptop.</p></div><div><h3>Host / local collaboration</h3><p>Access to fabrication tools and materials, projector and audiovisual equipment, technical support, local networks and site permissions where required.</p></div></div><small>Intended outcomes: a functional, collectively usable iteration of the archive and at least one site-responsive interactive installation. Final format remains responsive to local context and collaboration.</small></div></section>
  <section id="references" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">05 / SELECTED REFERENCES</span><div><h2>Conceptual coordinates</h2><ol><li>Gilles Deleuze & Félix Guattari, <em>A Thousand Plateaus: Capitalism and Schizophrenia</em> (1980; English translation 1987). — Rhizomatic thinking.</li><li>Donna J. Haraway, <em>Staying with the Trouble: Making Kin in the Chthulucene</em> (2016). — Situated relationships and more-than-human worlds.</li><li>Stefano Harney & Fred Moten, <em>The Undercommons: Fugitive Planning & Black Study</em> (2013). — Collective study and self-organisation.</li><li>Stavros Stavrides, <em>Common Space: The City as Commons</em> (2016). — Commoning and shared urban space.</li><li>Shannon Mattern, <em>A City Is Not a Computer: Other Urban Intelligences</em> (2021). — Critical approaches to urban data and infrastructure.</li></ol><small>Research background: <a href="https://thearchiveoftheuntamed.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Archive of the Untamed</a>.</small></div></section>
  <footer class="hyper-footer"><span>OTHERWISE HYPERARCHIVE / WORKING PROPOSAL / 2027</span><a href="#top">BACK TO TOP ↑</a></footer>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.hyperarchive{--hyper-line:var(--line,#555);--hyper-accent:var(--signal,#ff71c3);width:100%;font:12px/1.65 "Courier New",monospace;color:var(--fg)}
.hyperarchive *{box-sizing:border-box}.hyperarchive a{color:inherit}.hyper-top,.hyper-footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line);font-size:10px}.hyper-hero{padding:70px 0 55px;min-height:52vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-hero>span,.hyper-hero small,.hyper-index,.hyper-diagram figcaption,.hyperarchive small{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.07em;opacity:.75}.hyper-hero h1{font:400 clamp(34px,6.3vw,110px)/.96 "Courier New",monospace;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:35px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.hyper-accent{color:var(--hyper-accent)}.hyper-hero p{font-size:clamp(13px,1.4vw,17px)}.hyper-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(130px,24%) minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;padding:34px 0 48px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-section>div{max-width:1000px}.hyper-section h2{font:400 clamp(18px,2.2vw,30px)/1.2 "Courier New",monospace;margin:0 0 24px}.hyper-section h3{font:400 12px "Courier New",monospace;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 12px}.hyper-section p{font:inherit;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 15px}.hyper-columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.hyper-diagram{position:relative;border:1px solid var(--hyper-line);margin:22px 0;overflow:hidden;padding:28px 6px 6px}.hyper-diagram figcaption{position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px}.hyper-diagram svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;min-height:160px}.hyper-diagram svg text{fill:var(--fg);font:10px "Courier New",monospace}.hyper-diagram .wires{stroke:var(--fg);opacity:.5;stroke-dasharray:3 7;fill:none}.hyper-diagram .nodes{stroke:var(--hyper-accent);fill:var(--bg);stroke-width:1.2}.hyper-diagram .accent-wires{fill:none;stroke:var(--hyper-accent);stroke-width:1.5}.hyper-steps{margin:30px 0}.hyper-steps p{display:grid;grid-template-columns:75px 1fr;gap:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--hyper-line);padding:12px 0;margin:0}.hyper-steps strong{color:var(--hyper-accent);font-weight:400}.hyper-section ol{padding-left:20px}.hyper-section li{margin:0 0 10px}.hyper-footer{border:0;margin-top:30px}.hyperarchive :target{scroll-margin-top:24px}
html[data-portfolio-mode="institutional"] .hyperarchive{--hyper-accent:#222;--hyper-line:#aaa}
@media(max-width:760px){.hyper-section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:15px}.hyper-columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hyper-hero{min-height:40vh;padding:40px 0}.hyper-top,.hyper-footer{flex-direction:column}}
</style>
